[Music]  road to zero  improving road safety in waimakariri  the waimakariri district is one of the  fastest growing districts in the country  we have roughly 1500 kilometres of roads  that connect our urban and rural  communities  we have a vision for our community  where everyone can get around safely no  matter where and how you travel  road to zero  new zealand's road safety strategy has a  vision that no one is killed or  seriously injured on our roads  it acknowledges that despite our best  efforts crashes will still happen but no  one should be killed or seriously  injured as a result  every person killed or seriously injured  is somebody's family friend or loved one  the impacts of a crash can be  devastating  we all need to work together to make our  community a place where people can get  where they're going safely  whether they're walking cycling  driving riding a motorbike or using  public transport  we have spoken with people in the  community about road safety  listen to their stories in our road to  zero video series and tell us what you  think about the proposed changes to the  speed limits

